    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Fix boo#1235893 (CVE-2025-23386): generate and edit the config files
  in %post as the gerbera user (via runuser) instead of letting root
  write into the gerbera-owned /etc/gerbera directory. The previous fix
  only chowned that directory to root for the duration of %post, so
  symlinks staged there before the transaction were still followed by
  root.
  - Add Requires(post): util-linux for runuser.
  - Drop the use of sudo in %post, which was never a dependency of this
    package.
- Set a restrictive umask so generated config files have mode 0640.
- Pass --home to gerbera --create-config/--create-example-config, so the
  generated &lt;home&gt; no longer depends on the home directory of the user
  running %post.
</comment>
